CORE
break_linear_growth1.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.lz_break == 64 == main\.a == 0: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.lz_break == 64 \|\| .*: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.lz_return == main\.lz_break: PROVED up to bound 0$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A conditional break or return in an unrolled loop keeps the values that
the loop computes linear in the number of iterations. The leading-zero
count follows a priority encoder in PLENA (clz_int); before, the
expression for the count doubled with every iteration.
